Meotf lc-royrsgtalnlicnef amicerwooprokrso(usM/mOeFso)paorreoauns maetregrianlgs tlhasast tions involving catalysis1–3, gas storage4–6, water harvesting7–9, and energy devices10–12. MOFs are considered promising candidates for membrane gas separations, which are energy-efficient processes that can be applied for the treatment of flue gas (separation of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2})$ , the purification of natural gas (separation of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4},$ ) or hydrocarbons (separation of olefin/paraffin). The previous studies suggest that a membrane with a selectivity of over 30 (for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ or $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}\mathrm{\cdot}$ ) and a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeance of over 1000 GPU can reduce the cost of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ capture to 20–30 $\mathrm{US}\$123$ . MOFs can be processed in the form of mixed matrix membranes (MMMs) or pure MOF membranes for gas separations. Many MOF-based MMMs have shown good separation performance although they still need to be transformed to thin film composite membranes for industrial application. The MMM with Y-fum-fcu-MOF in 6FDA-DAM polyimide was reported to have a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity of approximately 30 with a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of nearly 1000 Barrer14,15. Hybrid UiO-66- $\mathrm{CN}@\mathrm{{sPIM-1}}$ membranes possessed a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ selectivity of roughly 55 with a permeability of about 12,000 Barrer16. NUS-8 nanosheets/PIM-1 membranes with $2\mathrm{wt\%}$ of the MOF exhibited a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity of approximately 30 and a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of nearly 6500 Barrer17. Hybrid Mg-MOF-74/PIM-1 membranes with $20\mathrm{wt\%}$ of MOF showed a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ selectivity of roughly 30 with $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of about 11,000 Barrer18.
Different from MOF-based MMMs, relatively few pure MOF membranes showed good separation performance for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ or $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ . IRMOF-1 membranes achieved $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity of over 300 with a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of $10,000\ \mathrm{Barrer^{19}}$ . MIL-160/CAU-10-F membranes have reached $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivities greater than 30 and 70, respectively. The $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of the MIL-160/CAU-10-F membranes was approximately 2,000 Barrer20. ZIF-94 membranes showed a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity of nearly 38 with a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of about 28 Barrer21. In addition to the experimental studies in MOF-based membranes for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ separations22–28, computational works have also been conducted to identify promising materials for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ separation29,30 and to investigate the mechanism for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ transport within $\mathrm{MOFs}^{31-33}$ .
In previous study, CAU-10-H, represent by the chemical formula $[\mathrm{Al(OH)BDC)}]$ ·solvent $({\mathrm{BDC~}}=$ benzene-1,3-dicarboxylic acid), was first reported by Reinsch et al.34. The inorganic building unit (IBU) of CAU-10-H has helical ${\mathrm{AlO}}_{6}$ polyhedra chains that share cis-corner OH- anions and bidentate carboxylate groups in their linker molecules. The structure of CAU-10-H comprised onedimensional channels along $c$ -axis, with a pore-limiting diameter (PLD) equaled to $3.2\mathring\mathrm{A}$ , which is comparable to the kinetic diameter of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ , ${\mathrm{N}}_{2},$ and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}{}^{35}$ . Recently, our group fabricated dense CAU-10-H membranes with a high $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity (up to 50) and a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of 220 Barrer35. After that work, CAU-10- PDC, a derivative compound to CAU-10-H with BDC replaced by pyridine-3,5-dicarboxylic acid (PDC) as a linker, have been processed to a dense membrane for similar applications36. In addition, the structural similarity between CAU-10-H and CAU-10-PDC was verified through structure refinement, suggesting that both structures belong to the same space group36. The pure CAU-10- PDC membrane achieved a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity of over 60 with a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ permeability of over 20 Barrer. However, a severe structural deformation was found for the CAU-10-PDC membrane under exposure to $\mathrm{CH}_{4}.$ , which led to a pronounced change in the PLD from 4.15 to $2.95\mathring\mathrm{A}$ .
The structural flexibility of MOFs significantly affects their applications to membrane gas separations. The rigid structure of ZIF-8 has a PLD of about $\partial.40\mathring\mathrm{A},$ and the pure ZIF-8 membranes had been expected to possess a high selectivity of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ (kinetic diameter, KD, of $3.30\mathring\mathrm{A}\mathrm{\cdot}$ ) over $\Nu_{2}$ (KD of $3.64\mathring{\mathrm{A}}\dot{\mathrm{.}}$ ) or $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ (KD of $3.80\mathring{\mathrm{A}})^{37}$ . Interestingly, most reported pure ZIF-8 membranes showed low selectivity for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ , but exhibited a very high selectivity of $\mathrm{C_{3}H_{6}/C_{3}\mathrm{\bar{H}_{8}}}$ (over $300)^{38-41}$ . This suggests that the effective aperture size of ZIF-8 is about $4.0{-}4.2\mathrm{\AA}.$ instead of $3.40\mathrm{\AA}$ . Follow-up studies suggest that those findings can be attributed to the linker rotation in ZIF-8, which enlarges the window size of the MOF for gas separations37,42–48. Recently, a rapid heat treatment (RHT) on the ZIF-8 membrane was developed to suppress the lattice flexibility49. Following the RHT, the pure ZIF-8 membrane can achieve a $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ selectivity of over 20. In different studies a mixed-linker approach has been used to suppress the gate-opening effects in ZIF-850,51.
Herein we propose a mixed-linker approach to suppress the structural flexibility of the CAU-10-based membranes, which can enhance the stability of the membranes during gas permeation tests. While the pure CAU-10-PDC membrane possesses good $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ selectivity (over 60), it struggled with severe structural deformation under exposure to $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ . In this work, we partially replaced PDC with BDC to improve the lattice rigidity of the membrane. We synthesized mixed-linker CAU-10-PDC-H membranes with the mixed-ligand strategy in different PDC-to-BDC ratios, as shown in Fig. 1. The samples were subject to comprehensive characterization with nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy, elemental analysis (EA), and scanning electron microscopy (SEM). We conducted single- and mixed-gas tests on the CAU-10-PDC-H membranes to evaluate their gas separation performance for $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{N}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ . X-ray diffraction (XRD) and diffuse reflectance infrared Fourier transform (DRIFT) spectroscopy were performed in situ under $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ to probe the structural deformation of the CAU-10-PDC-H. Computations based on the density functional theory (DFT) and energy decomposition analysis (EDA) were performed to support the experimental findings.
